  "description": "RONGIN crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group A b a 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C174 H148 Gd5 N26 Ni4 O44 1+,13.6(C2 H3 N1),0.5(H2 O1),Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.197-4.235 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.84-123.24°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni4Gd5(PhCOO)10(HL)4(HLzw)4(OH)2(NO3)2]Cl·13.6MeCN·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ni(II), Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
